# FUTURE — nice-to-have follow-ups (project shell)

- Dark mode: the night-study ladder is designed in
  `packages/design-tokens/src/ink-jade.css` (header comment). It needs a theme toggle and `.dark`
  overrides for the full token set, not just the shell ladder.
- PaneHeader chip seating: the centered chat title chip sizes itself `h-9` against the h-10 band
  because PaneHeader centers its title slot, while ContextTabBar seats chips with `items-stretch`.
  One adaptive band-chip geometry would mean no consumer knows the band height.
- Chats as a working-set tab strip: multiple chat tabs and a "+" in the centered chat band. Needs an
  "open chats" model (close ≠ delete, overflow, ordering) and a decision on how chat navigation
  relates to the sidebar.
- Bounded live sessions for restored desks (#217): the persisted desk restores every open tab, and
  the session registry keeps a live websocket-subscribed Y.Doc per tab, so a 30-tab desk means 30
  live sessions on every reload. Editor views are already bounded by `MAX_MOUNTED_EDITORS`. Move:
  lazy-connect background tabs' sessions on first view, with the same LRU shape. The Yjs FAQ warns
  against hydrating many Y.Docs.
- Multi-pane Editor layout: a split-view design first defines focus, history, tab membership and
  session retention; stretching the single-selection workspace reducer into two implicit selections
  won't hold.
- Work page tab search: switching between Chats and Files resets each tab's search. Keeping it means
  putting the Work chat search in the project address, as the chat index does with `q`.
